# Problem:
#   Predict probability of FIRST adoption of Drug XYZ in Q11 for
#   the 1,502 physicians in test_physicians.csv.
#
# IMPORTANT LEAKAGE RULES USED HERE
# ---------------------------------
# 1. test_physicians.csv is NEVER used to fit preprocessing, scaling,
#    imputation, clustering, model selection, or target-derived features.
# 2. physician-level train/validation split is performed BEFORE any
#    supervised EDA/model fitting.
# 3. rx_count is used ONLY to construct the training target and is
#    NEVER used as a predictor.
# 4. Target-derived territory adoption rate is calculated from TRAIN
#    physicians only and then mapped to validation/test.
# 5. K-Means is fitted on TRAIN physicians only.
# 6. Imputation, scaling, encoding and SMOTE are fitted/applied only
#    inside the training side of each model fit.
# 7. Final model is selected using validation performance, then refit
#    on all labelled training physicians before Q11 prediction.
#
# Expected input files:
#   input_data_file1.csv
#   input_data_file2.csv
#   test_physicians.csv
#
# If filenames differ, the script automatically searches the working
# directory for CSVs and identifies them using their columns.
#
# Outputs:
